WEBVTT

00:15.280 --> 00:24.883
MISSION: YOZAKURA FAMILY

01:31.600 --> 01:34.940
PLAN 20
SUN EARRINGS

01:34.940 --> 01:37.862
<i>If we let Tanpopo's influence
keep spreading,</i>

01:37.862 --> 01:40.242
<i>they're going to get
to Mutsumi eventually.</i>

01:40.868 --> 01:42.037
<i>Before that can happen...</i>

01:43.081 --> 01:44.501
<i>I'm going to stop it right here!</i>

01:47.590 --> 01:48.926
Viper's Nest.

01:54.353 --> 01:56.023
Yozakura Ancient Sword Technique...

01:57.777 --> 01:59.363
Spiral Autumn Shower!

02:01.409 --> 02:03.246
<i>I'll use this stun gun
to make her pass out.</i>

02:03.706 --> 02:04.541
Serpent.

02:15.605 --> 02:19.988
You can slice it away all you want,
but my hair will keep growing.

02:21.199 --> 02:22.201
Python.

02:28.379 --> 02:29.716
<i>How fierce is this attack?</i>

02:30.217 --> 02:32.597
<i>I can't even see it
unless I focus with all my might.</i>

02:36.020 --> 02:37.565
<i>Taiyo...</i>

02:38.441 --> 02:42.241
<i>I'm using my hair to simulate words,
to send this message to you...</i>

02:43.159 --> 02:47.209
<i>at a speed that would just be barely
discernable to vision enhanced to the max.</i>

02:48.253 --> 02:52.177
<i>Since we can't risk Dr. Kawashita
catching on to existing codes...</i>

02:52.887 --> 02:55.893
<i>it's safest to go
with this primitive method.</i>

02:56.770 --> 03:00.360
<i>This is happening
too fast for you to grasp, I'm sure.</i>

03:02.447 --> 03:07.249
<i>But this is the only way
that I can l let you know the truth</i>

03:07.249 --> 03:08.752
<i>in the time that I have left.</i>

03:09.420 --> 03:11.340
<i>So please listen carefully.</i>

03:12.927 --> 03:17.311
<i>It's my fault that your family died.</i>

03:26.287 --> 03:28.834
<i>It was more than ten years ago.</i>

03:31.464 --> 03:35.430
<i>Back then, my greatest wish...</i>

03:36.057 --> 03:37.602
<i>was to live.</i>

03:48.832 --> 03:49.834
Yuki!

03:51.379 --> 03:52.924
Ms. Akari?

03:52.924 --> 03:54.594
Happy Birthday!

03:55.095 --> 03:56.097
Congrats!

03:56.640 --> 03:59.938
My birthday?
You mean you actually remembered?

03:59.938 --> 04:01.399
Of course we did!

04:01.399 --> 04:03.444
Go on. Open it up.

04:05.866 --> 04:06.827
These are--

04:07.327 --> 04:12.295
The sun earrings we all said
were so lovely the other day!

04:14.634 --> 04:16.722
Why would you do this for me?

04:17.515 --> 04:19.226
What are you talking about?

04:19.226 --> 04:21.147
She's right, Yuki.

04:21.147 --> 04:23.652
Your long hospital stay
will be over in a bit,

04:23.986 --> 04:25.029
so let's keep fighting.

04:26.449 --> 04:28.411
Thank you so much.

04:34.632 --> 04:38.264
Now, now, save those happy tears
for when you're discharged!

04:38.264 --> 04:39.224
Right!

04:39.726 --> 04:43.065
It feels like we have a daughter now.

04:43.065 --> 04:45.445
I mean, both of our kids are boys.

04:46.489 --> 04:48.326
Well, it's lively in here again today, eh?

04:48.660 --> 04:50.246
Dr. Kawashita!

04:50.246 --> 04:53.169
And, Ms. Shirai,
you seem to be coming along nicely.

04:53.670 --> 04:57.970
It's all thanks to you
for suggesting the clinical trial.

04:57.970 --> 04:59.933
Thank you so much!

04:59.933 --> 05:01.268
I should be thanking you.

05:01.268 --> 05:04.651
I couldn't be more thrilled to see
such positive effects from the trial.

05:05.109 --> 05:06.696
Perhaps you'd like to wipe your nose?

05:06.696 --> 05:07.824
Oh, I'm sorry.

05:09.326 --> 05:13.627
By the way, Mr. Asano,
Dr. Fukuhara has been looking for you.

05:13.627 --> 05:17.593
Oh, whoops!
I forgot I was here to do some marketing!

05:17.593 --> 05:19.973
All right,
I guess I'll be leaving, too, Yuki.

05:20.558 --> 05:22.770
If you'll excuse us, Dr. Kawashita.

05:22.979 --> 05:25.526
Right. Thank you very much.

05:27.070 --> 05:28.489
Thanks for all your hard work.

05:32.957 --> 05:34.376
Where did you get those?

05:35.086 --> 05:37.132
They're such beautiful earrings.

05:37.132 --> 05:40.263
The Asanos gave them to me as a present.

05:40.263 --> 05:44.856
Oh, really? They must
really like you a lot, Ms. Shirai.

05:45.524 --> 05:48.112
As if you were really family.

06:09.488 --> 06:11.200
Look at that, Yuki! It's a rainbow.

06:11.701 --> 06:14.248
You're right. So lovely.

06:14.916 --> 06:17.253
You really put up a good fight, Yuki.

06:17.253 --> 06:20.009
That just... makes me so happy.

06:23.474 --> 06:24.434
Yuki...

06:25.061 --> 06:28.568
from now on,
you're going to do what you love,

06:28.568 --> 06:32.158
dress up, study with your classmates,
make new friends,

06:32.158 --> 06:33.912
meet wonderful people along the way.

06:34.539 --> 06:37.419
Let's make lots and lots
of beautiful memories...

06:37.962 --> 06:39.381
here, under the sun.

06:41.427 --> 06:44.851
<i>I was so thrilled and happy...</i>

06:46.270 --> 06:50.153
<i>until I found out that it was all a lie.</i>

06:52.950 --> 06:55.455
FIRST MEMORIAL HOSPITAL
Hey, Ms. Shirai. Long time no see!

06:55.455 --> 06:57.835
It's been a while, Dr. Kawashita.

06:58.335 --> 07:01.133
Yeah. Looks like
you're making good progress.

07:01.634 --> 07:03.764
I owe it all to you.

07:03.764 --> 07:07.145
I never dreamed
that I'd be able to walk again on my own.

07:07.646 --> 07:09.942
It still feels like a dream to me.

07:09.942 --> 07:14.911
Well, your desire to live
beat your illness, that's all.

07:16.080 --> 07:17.457
Thank you so much!

07:18.960 --> 07:21.423
Oh, hold on, Ms. Shirai.

07:21.800 --> 07:23.595
Do you have some time now?

07:24.096 --> 07:26.601
There's something
that I'd like to show you.

07:33.155 --> 07:35.953
I've injected ten thousand or so
test subjects with Hazakura

07:35.953 --> 07:38.792
over the last few years
and kept tabs on their progress,

07:38.792 --> 07:41.923
but most of them ended up expiring
after a year or two.

07:41.923 --> 07:44.929
But by some miracle,
the Hazakura side effects

07:44.929 --> 07:48.812
seemed to complement
the effects of your illness,

07:48.812 --> 07:52.152
and so you're the only one
with 100% compatibility who's survived.

07:55.742 --> 07:59.917
Hey, it's not like this is some
shady experiment by an evil organization.

08:00.669 --> 08:06.388
By continuing our research,
we can offer salvation to those like you.

08:07.098 --> 08:10.354
It's the result of love,
ideals, and hard work.

08:14.029 --> 08:16.241
Wh-What about the Asanos?

08:16.576 --> 08:18.622
Don't worry. I saw to it

08:18.622 --> 08:22.713
that they departed this world
as upstanding people who knew nothing.

08:23.047 --> 08:24.174
What?

08:24.550 --> 08:28.140
Along with the rest of their family
so they wouldn't be lonely.

08:32.106 --> 08:33.150
<i>Yuki!</i>

08:33.818 --> 08:34.779
<i>Yuki!</i>

08:35.488 --> 08:36.574
<i>Yuki!</i>

08:37.116 --> 08:38.077
<i>Yuki!</i>

08:38.745 --> 08:39.580
<i>Yuki!</i>

08:39.580 --> 08:41.208
<i>- Yuki! Yuki!
- Yuki!</i>

08:41.208 --> 08:42.544
<i>- Yuki!
- Yuki!</i>

08:43.546 --> 08:47.513
Whoops. So once it starts rotting,
I guess it's all over.

08:49.892 --> 08:51.980
To make sure
that no evidence is left behind...

08:52.480 --> 08:55.696
we eliminate all who were involved.

08:56.864 --> 09:02.166
Someone else's noble sacrifices,
that's what keeps this world going.

09:03.586 --> 09:05.882
This life that you gained
thanks to them...

09:06.968 --> 09:08.345
take good care of it, all right?

09:11.101 --> 09:13.314
<i>Welcome to Tanpopo.</i>

09:14.190 --> 09:18.240
<i>I'd like to give you an alias
based on that gorgeous white hair.</i>

09:18.240 --> 09:19.577
<i>How about Hakuja?</i>

09:25.421 --> 09:28.637
<i>This is the gift
that your parents gave me.</i>

09:29.680 --> 09:34.481
<i>They've been modified and fitted with GPS
to monitor my comings and goings.</i>

09:35.483 --> 09:38.364
<i>Meaning that you can use them
to track down</i>

09:38.364 --> 09:41.370
<i>the evil forces
that are targeting your family.</i>

09:45.712 --> 09:50.304
<i>As someone who chose to go down
a dark path, I have no right to wear them.</i>

09:51.557 --> 09:54.354
<i>Yes, this is my penance</i>

09:54.354 --> 09:58.445
<i>for sacrificing so many others
so that I could live selfishly.</i>

09:58.988 --> 10:04.917
<i>This is my request to you,
a member of the Yozakura spy family.</i>

10:09.134 --> 10:10.094
<i>Taiyo?</i>

10:10.887 --> 10:11.848
<i>Taiyo!</i>

10:12.641 --> 10:14.102
<i>Big Bro!</i>

10:14.352 --> 10:17.693
<i>I want you to find a clue
that will protect your family</i>

10:17.693 --> 10:22.326
<i>from the hands of the woman
who robbed you of your family.</i>

10:37.691 --> 10:39.737
You hang in there, okay?

10:39.737 --> 10:42.200
Honey, I'm going to save--

10:42.200 --> 10:43.828
- Come on!
- Hang on!

10:44.622 --> 10:45.498
Don't let go of her!

10:45.498 --> 10:47.335
You can't swim,
so what are you doing, Dad?

10:47.335 --> 10:48.713
You can do it! Come on!

10:51.051 --> 10:54.182
Thank you so much for saving my daughter!

10:54.182 --> 10:56.854
Sorry to ruin your precious family time.

10:57.063 --> 10:58.440
Thank you so much!

10:58.900 --> 11:01.948
Now, now, you'd do the same for us.

11:01.948 --> 11:02.783
Where's Dad?

11:03.158 --> 11:03.993
All messed up.

11:03.993 --> 11:04.829
WIPED OUT

11:05.120 --> 11:07.333
Well, I'm a nurse, after all.

11:07.333 --> 11:09.295
So this is just normal for me!

11:09.797 --> 11:11.216
<i>"Normal,"</i>

11:11.216 --> 11:13.805
<i>that was my mom's
favorite turn of phrase.</i>

11:14.640 --> 11:16.936
<i>He may have been a wimp,
but you could depend on Dad.</i>

11:17.604 --> 11:18.857
<i>Kindhearted Hikaru.</i>

11:20.401 --> 11:23.866
<i>I loved this family of mine
that was just a little too well-meaning,</i>

11:23.866 --> 11:24.952
<i>and I was proud of it.</i>

11:26.914 --> 11:27.958
<i>My family...</i>

11:28.458 --> 11:30.797
<i>my... normal...</i>

11:33.970 --> 11:35.849
<i>Hikaru?</i>

11:40.984 --> 11:45.994
<i>I couldn't... preserve my "normal."</i>

11:47.539 --> 11:51.338
<i>I never knew that I'd grow to love
the kindness I was shown</i>

11:51.338 --> 11:53.801
<i>or the meaningless conversations we had.</i>

11:54.511 --> 11:58.686
<i>Just like we could have a fight,
but then make up the next day,</i>

11:59.187 --> 12:04.865
<i>I thought that I'd be able to say
good night and good morning forever.</i>

12:06.409 --> 12:10.835
<i>I keep losing the people I care about
because I'm weak.</i>

12:20.897 --> 12:25.740
My comrades waiting at the station
will be retrieving the Hazakura soon.

12:27.034 --> 12:30.040
I'm sorry, but I'll be disembarking now.

12:37.179 --> 12:39.350
Well, would you look at that?

12:39.643 --> 12:42.106
His body temp's rising,
his abilities are being enhanced,

12:42.106 --> 12:43.609
his reflexes are improving,

12:43.609 --> 12:46.156
and his stats are soaring
like it's a glitch in the system!

12:46.699 --> 12:49.913
Is this true Yozakura power?

12:49.913 --> 12:54.005
No, he's losing control of the someinine
due to his strong passions.

12:54.506 --> 12:57.554
Someinine increases or decreases
depending on one's emotions,

12:57.554 --> 12:58.723
which makes it powerful,

12:58.723 --> 13:01.896
but that's what makes it
far more dangerous than Hazakura.

13:01.896 --> 13:06.279
He's already gone past the level at which
someone of his proficiency can control it.

13:06.279 --> 13:10.872
The someinine activation will destroy
his body in the next few minutes,

13:10.872 --> 13:12.374
and it will kill him.

13:23.940 --> 13:28.490
As your power and speed increase,
your accuracy is trending downward.

13:28.991 --> 13:32.206
There's no more useful data
that can be extracted from you.

13:32.707 --> 13:35.212
In which direction
would you like to be hurled?

13:35.922 --> 13:38.176
Goodbye, Taiyo.

13:43.813 --> 13:45.023
<i>Hikaru.</i>

13:46.317 --> 13:47.319
<i>Dad.</i>

13:48.446 --> 13:49.490
<i>Mom.</i>

13:50.450 --> 13:51.327
<i>Sorry.</i>

13:52.204 --> 13:53.123
<i>I...</i>

13:54.375 --> 13:55.252
<i>I...</i>

13:58.341 --> 13:59.845
<i>Taiyo.</i>

14:08.571 --> 14:10.617
<i>Why are you...</i>

14:14.875 --> 14:16.294
<i>Well, of course.</i>

14:18.925 --> 14:21.387
<i>Isn't that just normal?</i>

14:35.415 --> 14:37.336
Impressive that you
managed to free yourself.

14:37.754 --> 14:41.427
But with that body of yours,
barely able to even control it...

14:46.479 --> 14:48.233
His own leg?

14:48.233 --> 14:50.195
Has going berserk made him crazy?

14:50.195 --> 14:51.155
That's bloodletting.

14:52.074 --> 14:54.161
A way to adjust
the excess buildup of someinine

14:54.161 --> 14:57.251
by removing it, blood and all.

14:57.251 --> 14:59.631
A primitive stopgap measure
that takes advantage

14:59.631 --> 15:02.344
of his body's immense regenerative power.

15:02.344 --> 15:04.599
Shinzo's advice, I suppose?

15:04.808 --> 15:08.566
<i>That day, I couldn't preserve my "normal."</i>

15:10.402 --> 15:12.741
<i>But it's different now.</i>

15:16.080 --> 15:20.338
I'm going to protect this "normal"
where Mutsumi and the others live!

15:22.051 --> 15:27.102
<i>You send Yae's current to your cells
and increase the someinine's conductivity.</i>

15:27.604 --> 15:32.906
<i>But a single shot is your max right now,
Taiyo, so only use it...</i>

15:34.366 --> 15:36.329
<i>to seal your victory.</i>

15:41.130 --> 15:43.719
<i>That's the spirit, Taiyo.</i>

15:46.182 --> 15:47.727
Eight-headed Serpent.

15:51.442 --> 15:53.071
Yozakura Ancient Sword Technique...

16:00.545 --> 16:01.922
Amaterasu!

16:08.393 --> 16:12.652
<i>In the end, I lost everything.</i>

16:15.616 --> 16:17.369
<i>Such gorgeous hair.</i>

16:17.954 --> 16:19.875
<i>Those earrings look good on you, too.</i>

16:23.214 --> 16:28.601
<i>I went so far as to sacrifice
such lovely people as them to obtain it.</i>

16:39.664 --> 16:43.839
You couldn't bring yourself
to turn on me right 'til the end.

16:44.340 --> 16:48.264
You really are too nice, aren't you?

16:56.364 --> 16:57.241
What?

16:58.535 --> 17:01.667
Mom and Dad mentioned you a lot.

17:02.292 --> 17:05.423
That there was a girl hanging in there
despite her illness and treatment,

17:05.423 --> 17:06.677
without a word of complaint.

17:08.012 --> 17:14.693
This girl's hands were warm and kind
and bursting with compassion.

17:15.360 --> 17:18.074
They said she was a girl
who could set everyone at ease

17:18.074 --> 17:20.663
and that she had hands like the sun.

17:23.084 --> 17:26.800
It was just Tanpopo using people
who were trying so hard to live.

17:27.426 --> 17:30.307
My family's deaths weren't your fault.

17:32.185 --> 17:36.528
Thank you for holding on
to my parents' keepsake all this time.

17:37.572 --> 17:41.329
Thanks to you, this time,
I'll be able to protect my family.

17:51.015 --> 17:52.392
<i>Ms. Akari.</i>

17:53.227 --> 17:54.313
<i>Mr. Hide.</i>

17:55.816 --> 17:57.235
<i>I have no...</i>

18:06.713 --> 18:08.884
I've got to stop this train.

18:15.940 --> 18:17.401
<i>Another enemy?</i>

18:19.906 --> 18:21.158
<i>A kid?</i>

18:25.208 --> 18:26.962
Well done, Ms. Ai!

18:27.462 --> 18:28.799
Mr. Mizuki!

18:29.133 --> 18:32.557
But didn't I teach you
to go for the head when you hunt?

18:33.057 --> 18:36.313
That isn't enough to wipe out
the Yozakura blood, you know.

18:38.484 --> 18:41.742
I'm sorry. I really stink.

18:41.742 --> 18:42.952
No, no.

18:43.494 --> 18:45.833
I'm not angry with you.

18:45.833 --> 18:47.712
You're an amazing child, Ms. Ai.

18:48.212 --> 18:50.175
Let's keep working, little by little.

18:53.097 --> 18:54.642
I'm going to give it my all!

18:55.770 --> 18:56.605
Now, then...

18:57.314 --> 19:01.573
as Mr. Kawashita ordered, let's retrieve
the Hazakura and Ms. Hakuja's body.

19:04.077 --> 19:05.288
As well as...

19:05.288 --> 19:07.543
dispose of the sample
that we have no more use for.

19:12.219 --> 19:14.974
Don't worry. I'll put you
out of your misery right away.

19:19.066 --> 19:22.405
Sorry, Ms. Rin,
for making you come with me.

19:22.657 --> 19:24.451
Hey, no problem!

19:25.036 --> 19:28.125
I owe Taiyo one
for that Kuroyuri incident,

19:28.125 --> 19:31.131
and it's been a while
since we battled together like this.

19:31.131 --> 19:34.471
Remember when we tore
that moron eldest son a new one?

19:34.471 --> 19:38.145
We did that so often,
I'm not sure which time you mean.

19:38.145 --> 19:39.189
I hear you!

19:39.481 --> 19:41.151
Big Sis Futaba!

19:41.695 --> 19:44.116
You're safe now, Taiyo.

19:44.324 --> 19:47.122
The Hinagiku chief
and the eldest Yozakura daughter.

19:47.122 --> 19:50.086
Who knew that the spy world's
two biggest female stars would show up?

19:54.846 --> 19:56.808
Hey! Ms. Ai, get back here!

20:06.786 --> 20:09.124
You can shake hands pretty well,
huh, little girl?

20:09.584 --> 20:11.504
Whoa!

20:11.796 --> 20:13.382
Stay, Ms. Ai.

20:17.182 --> 20:23.277
I get that you want to impress me, but
the goal of today's mission is not battle.

20:23.444 --> 20:25.156
I'm sorry.

20:26.158 --> 20:29.247
Those two are extreme specialists
in hand-to-hand combat.

20:29.666 --> 20:32.170
It wouldn't be wise
to charge them head-on.

20:33.130 --> 20:35.636
Fortunately, they don't do well...

20:37.055 --> 20:38.684
against my powers.

20:39.686 --> 20:41.355
Dead Man's Tongue.

20:46.908 --> 20:47.910
Poison, huh?

20:48.411 --> 20:50.164
Good for weeding the yard, right?

20:51.375 --> 20:52.460
Yeah, you got that right!

20:53.129 --> 20:55.466
All right, I'm gonna send you flying!

21:12.000 --> 21:14.046
<i>Dragon's Flower Breath.</i>

21:15.381 --> 21:18.680
One of these days,
I'll be extracting your data, too.

21:19.264 --> 21:21.603
I'm here to pick up my kid brother today.

21:22.145 --> 21:24.274
But I'll take you on
when I'm free sometime.

21:24.692 --> 21:25.527
All righty.

21:39.179 --> 21:41.810
Hey, thanks, Mizuki.

21:42.812 --> 21:43.897
You, too, Hakuja.

21:44.857 --> 21:45.859
Good work.

21:47.988 --> 21:49.366
Ms. Hakuja.

21:49.366 --> 21:51.871
She's all shriveled up, poor thing.

21:52.455 --> 21:55.127
But take a look at her face.

21:56.965 --> 21:58.885
She looks so at peace.

22:01.808 --> 22:06.609
Too bad, as far as Tanpopo intel goes,
we came up empty, huh?

22:06.609 --> 22:08.279
I wouldn't say that.

22:08.905 --> 22:12.997
This kid overcame even Kyoichiro
with just his heart.

22:13.748 --> 22:16.629
He may still be green
in terms of skills and experience,

22:16.629 --> 22:18.967
but I'm sure
that he got hold of something.

22:19.467 --> 22:22.015
That's the kind of kid he is.

22:23.560 --> 22:25.438
Big Sis... Futaba.

22:27.233 --> 22:29.404
Welcome back, Taiyo.

22:30.239 --> 22:32.118
Mission accomplished.

24:07.976 --> 24:12.485
NEXT TIME
YOZAKURA FRONT LINES / THE BLOOMING
